    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner API to return `contactPreference` = `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`. I implemented this following the existing derived-field pattern used for `locality`, `membershipLevel`, etc.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` string field to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time), next to `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Named(\"formatContactPreference\")` method returning `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner has a non-empty email and `\"PHONE\"` otherwise, and wired it via `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto`.\n\nBecause the value derives solely from the owner's email, computing it in the mapper (same as `membershipLevel`) is the natural fit \u2014 no controller/service changes needed.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (both `corePhoneWhenNoEmail` and `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n(This isn't a git repository, so there's nothing to commit.)",
